{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/789213-z-splats","id":789213,"title":"Z-Splats?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-19T05:42:53-08:00","id":789213,"title":"Z-Splats?","content":"I've heard it mentioned a few times now and then, but I'm not sure what sort of things it's referring to. I get x-splat and y-splat, but what are some examples of z-splats?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-19T05:48:07-08:00","id":789216,"title":"","content":"X: Auspice, Clan, Path<br /> Y: Tribe, Covenant, Order <br /> Z: Lodges, Bloodlines, Legacies<br /> <br /> It's that last, more selective group you can choose for your character, usually the one least integral to society as a whole and that has more stringent requirements to join.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","user":"Amravanti","date":". 12-19-2015, 09:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-19T06:55:18-08:00","id":789234,"title":"","content":"Not every supernatural template has a Z-splat, and some of them vary significantly in nature. For example, the Promethean's first edition Athanor has much less influence on the character than a typical vampiric bloodline or supernal Legacy, and the reenvisioned Athanor spoiled for second edition is a physical object made special to the character. Hunters and mummies don't really have anything very analogous at all, Sin-Eaters have customizable krewes that serve as a sort of communal do-it-yourself Z-splat, and demons and Beasts have attainable mechanics unique to the character (the Cipher and the Incarnate Inheritance) that fill a similar role without being predefined or shared with other characters in the world.<br /> <br /> In general, the &quot;Z-splat&quot; represents some optional stage of mechanical development, usually (but not always) attained later in a character's progression, that serves to flesh the character out in ways more particular and unique than the usually archetypal inborn X and ideological Y splats. The Z-splat is where you get into characters who are unusually specialized or dedicated to a certain field, or who represent strange offshoots or wield uncommon abilities that no amount of experience or study alone can quite duplicate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-19T07:24:01-08:00","id":789242,"title":"","content":"I wonder if minor templates should be considered mortal z-splats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-19T16:36:55-08:00","id":789472,"title":"","content":"Okay, that makes sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T10:00:47-07:00","id":975989,"title":"","content":"Hm... Would professions in Hunter not qualify as z-splats?<br /> <br /> Granted, they don't have a major mechanical impact on the game, but I'd been thinking about cobbling together a system that made them a more integral part of character development, just for fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","user":"dxanders","date":". 09-25-2016, 01:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T10:34:01-07:00","id":976005,"title":"","content":"I believe now they're just considered Merits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T13:19:25-07:00","id":976068,"title":"","content":"Z Splat: Anthors, Bloodlines, Legacies, Noble/Eldrich Entitlements, Lodges.<br /> <br /> Kiths are odd in the sense that they seem like a Z-Splat in function, but are extension of the X -Splat.<br /> <br /> For Changelings its:<br /> <br /> X Splats: Seeming<br /> Sub X splats: Kith<br /> Y Splats: Courts<br /> Z Splats: Noble/Eldrich Entitlements","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T13:33:36-07:00","id":976073,"title":"","content":"In a sense, the MCI merit is a universal customizable Z-Splat that you can have multiple of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T16:55:09-07:00","id":976168,"title":"","content":"There is no real formal definition of an X/Y/Z splat, anyway; they were terms that came up for a pattern that arose in the initial three then-nWoD gamelines, and each gameline that followed deviated from that pattern in some way. Even Promethean was the first game where the Y-splat ceased to be a political or social alliance, and became a mark of pure outlook and approach, as it would later represent in Demon and Beast.<br /> <br /> Worrying about how to fit the pattern isn't important, because the pattern isn't important. It's just one means of accomplishing what is important: offering something to characters that balances connection and definition with freedom and accessibility, in a way that's practical to present as part of the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T17:46:16-07:00","id":976191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/789213-z-splats?p=976068#post976068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Z Splat: Anthors, Bloodlines, Legacies, Noble/Eldrich Entitlements, Lodges.<br /> <br /> Kiths are odd in the sense that they seem like a Z-Splat in function, but are extension of the X -Splat.<br /> <br /> For Changelings its:<br /> <br /> X Splats: Seeming<br /> Sub X splats: Kith<br /> Y Splats: Courts<br /> Z Splats: Noble/Eldrich Entitlements</div> </div> </div> </div>With 2e, changeling seems more:<br /> X-Kiths<br /> Y-Seeming<br /> Z-Courts+Entitlements<br /> <br /> For proof the first chapter which is the X/Y splat chapter is about Kiths then Seemings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T18:41:18-07:00","id":976225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/789213-z-splats?p=976191#post976191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With 2e, changeling seems more:<br /> X-Kiths<br /> Y-Seeming<br /> Z-Courts+Entitlements<br /> <br /> For proof the first chapter which is the X/Y splat chapter is about Kiths then Seemings.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yeah good point mine really described 1e more, but with the change to Seemings making it something of a Y splat now, its pushed Courts into the Z Splat territory, the courts even kind of feel like Z splat. Of course what does that make Entitlements, the ZZ splat <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T19:15:26-07:00","id":976252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/789213-z-splats?p=976168#post976168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is no real formal definition of an X/Y/Z splat, anyway; they were terms that came up for a pattern that arose in the initial three then-nWoD gamelines, and each gameline that followed deviated from that pattern in some way. Even Promethean was the first game where the Y-splat ceased to be a political or social alliance, and became a mark of pure outlook and approach, as it would later represent in Demon and Beast.<br /> <br /> Worrying about how to fit the pattern isn't important, because the pattern isn't important. It's just one means of accomplishing what is important: offering something to characters that balances connection and definition with freedom and accessibility, in a way that's practical to present as part of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Agreed. I think a lot of players tend to focus a lot more on symmetry of mechanical concepts. I recognize that as it exists, occupations don't really fit the standard (and nor should they, necessarily, but I like the idea of establishing them more prominently, because I think they fit the core theme of the game really well, and they fill a mechanical niche that not everything does. The majority of the game follows the hunt, integrity rules manage the relationship between the hunt and your sanity, and I think more robust occupation rules could emphasize the lives of characters outside the hunt.<br /> <br /> I like occupation. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> And I think it would be cool to establish them as a more mechanically prominent part of a character concept in Hunter (which could emphasize the theme that all of these characters have lives outside the hunt). I'd consider adding a stat bonus beyond the specializations and ability buys and maybe a secondary ambition that allows more rapid development of beats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","user":"dxanders","date":". 09-25-2016, 10:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T00:27:16-07:00","id":976405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/789213-z-splats?p=976191#post976191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With 2e, changeling seems more:<br /> X-Kiths<br /> Y-Seeming<br /> Z-Courts+Entitlements<br /> <br /> For proof the first chapter which is the X/Y splat chapter is about Kiths then Seemings.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd be more inclined to consider Seeming to be a second X splat, rather than a Y. While Seeming is based on the character's choices, it isn't something that is decided upon specifically, barring a special Hedge quest to change it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T04:08:15-07:00","id":976456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/789213-z-splats?p=976168#post976168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is no real formal definition of an X/Y/Z splat, anyway; they were terms that came up for a pattern that arose in the initial three then-nWoD gamelines, and each gameline that followed deviated from that pattern in some way. Even Promethean was the first game where the Y-splat ceased to be a political or social alliance, and became a mark of pure outlook and approach, as it would later represent in Demon and Beast.</div> </div> </div> </div>Someone, I think it was Dataweaver, suggested that Y and Z should be redefined so that Y applied to social divisions (covenants, tribes, orders, courts, guilds), and Z to psychological ones (refinements, archetypes, agendas). (Beast and Deviant essentially have two X's). I liked the idea, because you kind of get the physical/social/mental division into splats along with atributes, skills, and merits.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T06:07:18-07:00","id":976486,"title":"","content":"I always thought of it as X = &quot;What am I?&quot;, Y = &quot;What do I do now/How do I handle this?&quot;, Z = A later extension of either X OR Y. So a Vampire's Bloodlines change primarily What Am I, and secondarily What Do I Do Now, especially in second edition. A Lodge changes primarily What Do I Do Now, while a Legacy is equal parts What Am I and What Do I Do Now, being a social group just as much as a refinement of the soul.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2291-gwyn-chan-r-gwyll","name":"Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}